<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Readymix first-half pre-tax profit up 85pct.</title>
<headline>Readymix first-half pre-tax profit up 85pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>					  (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		7.89		   vs 4.66</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.3		    vs 1.2</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    3.90		   vs 2.11</p>
<p> Turnover		   30.18		  vs 19.66</p>
<p> Operating profit	 3.88		   vs 2.08</p>
<p> Interest receivable    0.01		   vs 0.03</p>
<p> Tax charge		 0.60		   vs 0.25</p>
<p> Attributable	     3.30		   vs 1.86</p>
<p> Record date		September 24</p>
<p> Pay date		   October 7</p>
<p> Ex-dividend date	 September 16</p>
<p>NOTE - Irish-based building materials group Readymix Plc said the results for the half year indicated the continuing buoyant trading conditions in the Republic of Ireland, with strong growth in profits on both a product and geographical basis.</p>
<p>Readymix said margins had improved, due principally to higher volumes and tight cost control.</p>
<p>The group said trading in July and August confirmed the continuation of the trends of the earlier months.</p>
<p>-- Damien Lynch, Dublin Newsroom +353 1 6603377</p>
